---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';

const tracks = [
  {
    title: 'Ph.D.',
    body: [
      'Apply to the Department of Computer Science, Golisano College of Computing and Information Sciences at Rochester Institute of Technology, if you wish to work with me. If you are already at RIT, feel free to email me, schedule a meeting, or stop by my office.',
      'Prior research experience is required. Please read the Research experience section above before you write, and describe yours in your email.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Research Intern',
    body: [
      'Both remote and in-person interns are welcome. Openings come up throughout the year, sometimes on a monthly basis, and are filled case by case. Send your CV with a short note on what you would like to work on, and I will keep you in mind for the next suitable project. High school students are welcome to apply as well.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Capstone and Independent Study',
    body: [
      'If your degree program requires a capstone project, or you would like to do an independent study for credit, I am open to supervising projects in my research areas. Reach out early in the semester before you plan to start, with a short note on your program and the kind of project you have in mind.',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Layout title="Prospective Students | Zhiqian Chen">
  <main class="container">
    <Nav current="students" />

    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Prospective Students</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Please send your CV, transcript, and a short note on your research experience by email.
        <a class="email-btn" href="mailto:zhiqian.chen@rit.edu?subject=Prospective%20student" title="Email"><i class="fas fa-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i>Email me</a>
      </p>
      <p class="contact">I currently take Ph.D. students, research interns, and capstone or independent study students.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="email-note"><strong>In your email</strong>, please include two or three sentences on your research experience, with links, along with your CV and transcript. I read many inquiries, and I may not be able to follow up on emails that leave this out.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Basic requirements</h2>
      <ul class="reqs">
        <li>A background in engineering, computer science, mathematics or a related field</li>
        <li>Solid coding skills</li>
        <li>Solid mathematics</li>
        <li>Genuine passion and motivation for research</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="research-experience">
      <h2>Research experience (required)</h2>
      <p>A Ph.D. is a research degree, and the best sign that someone will thrive in one is that they have already done research. This is the one requirement I do not waive.</p>
      <ul class="reqs">
        <li><strong>The clearest evidence is a paper</strong>, published, accepted, or under review, to which you made a substantial contribution. A first-author paper at a strong venue in AI or your own field is ideal.</li>
        <li><strong>No paper yet? That can be fine</strong>, as long as you have done real research. Tell me concretely what question you worked on, what you did yourself, and what came out of it, such as a thesis, a preprint, a technical report, code, or a poster. A note from the person who supervised you helps.</li>
        <li>Coursework, course projects, and engineering-only internships usually do not count as research experience on their own.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you are still building research experience, a great way to start is an independent research project, beyond coursework, supervised by a faculty member. It can be at your own school, with my group (remote is welcome), or at any other institution.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Tracks</h2>
      <div class="tracks">
        {tracks.map((t) => (
          <article class="track">
            <h3>{t.title}</h3>
            {t.body.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
<style>
  :root { --accent:#C45200; --ink:#16202B; --muted:#4E5C6A; }
  .container { max-width: min(95vw, 1600px); margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; box-sizing: border-box; }

  .hero { margin: 10px 0 28px; }
  .hero h1 { font-family:'et-book',Palatino,serif; font-size:2rem; margin:0 0 8px; color:var(--ink); }
  .hero .lead { margin: 0 0 6px; color:#2E3A47; font-size:1rem; }
  .hero .contact { margin: 0; color:var(--muted); font-size:.92rem; }
  .hero .lead a, .hero .contact a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .hero .contact a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .hero .lead { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:8px 14px; }
  .hero .lead a.email-btn { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; padding:5px 14px; border-radius:6px; background:var(--accent); color:#fff; font-size:.88rem; font-weight:600; }
  .hero .lead a.email-btn:hover { background:#A84600; }

  .section { padding-top: 6px; margin-top: 22px; }
  .section h2 { font-family:'et-book',Palatino,serif; font-size:.82rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--accent); margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .section > p { color:#2E3A47; font-size:.95rem; line-height:1.55; margin: 0 0 10px; }

  .reqs { margin:0; padding-left:20px; color:#2E3A47; font-size:.95rem; line-height:1.7; text-align:left; }
  #research-experience .reqs { margin:0 0 12px; line-height:1.55; }
  .section > p.email-note { background:#FDF1E7; border-left:3px solid var(--accent); padding:8px 12px; }
  #research-experience .reqs li { margin-bottom:6px; }
  .tracks { display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 14px; }
  .track { background:#EEF3F8; padding:16px 18px; }
  .track h3 { font-family:'et-book',Palatino,serif; font-size:1.02rem; margin:0 0 8px; color:var(--ink); }
  .track p:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }
  .track p { text-align:left; margin:0 0 8px; color:#2E3A47; font-size:.92rem; line-height:1.55; }


  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .tracks { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
